for:
- Iterates over a fixed set of values;
- Runs a predefined number of times.

while:
- Runs while the condition is true;
- Useful when the number of iterations is unknown

until:
- Runs until the condition is true;
- Similar to while, but stops when the condition becomes true

Key Differences:
- for is best when looping over a known range or list (for i in {1..10} or for file in *.txt).
- while continues as long as the condition is true (while [ $x -lt 10 ]).
- until continues until the condition becomes true (until [ $x -ge 10 ]).
